{"name":"Blossom Powder","hex":"#c3b3b9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blossom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flower, especially one indicating that a fruit tree is fruiting;  a mass of such flowers.","The state or season of producing such flowers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have, or open into, blossoms; to bloom.","To begin to thrive or flourish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blossom"},{"term":"powder","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fine particles which are the result of reducing a dry substance by pounding, grinding, or triturating, or the result of decay; dust.\n\n Cocaine in powder form (as opposed to crack).","Cocaine in powder form (as opposed to crack)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reduce to fine particles; to pound, grind, or rub into a powder.","To sprinkle with powder, or as if with powder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/powder"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blossom","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, blossoms are the flowers of stone fruit trees and of some other plants with a similar appearance that flower profusely for a period of time in spring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png/330px-Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blossom"},{"title":"Powder","blocks":[{"text":"A powder is a dry solid composed of many very fine particles that may flow freely when shaken or tilted. Powders are a special sub-class of granular materials, although the terms powder and granular are sometimes used to distinguish separate classes of material. In particular, powders refer to those granular materials that have the finer grain sizes, and that therefore have a greater tendency to form clumps when flowing. Granulars refer to the coarser granular materials that do not tend to form clumps except when wet."}